$ Two square CBAR cantilevers with a torque at the tip and torsional stress coefficient C = a/2.
$ Elements 1-2: a = 5 mm, L = 100 mm, T = 1 N-m. Elements 3-4: the same scaled by 1/100, a = 50 um, L = 1 mm, T = 1E-6 N-m.
$ The small bar's J = 8.8E-19 m^4 is smaller than machine epsilon but is a real value that must be used as is.
$ Both bars have the same torsional stress T*C/J and the same twist T*L/(G*J).
SOL 101
CEND
TITLE = 101_bar_small_j_torsion
ECHO = NONE
SPC = 1
LOAD = 1
DISPLACEMENT = ALL
SPCFORCES = ALL
STRESS = ALL
ELFORCE = ALL
BEGIN BULK
PARAM,POST,-1
MAT1,1,2.E+11,,0.3,0.,0.,0.0
PBAR,1,1,2.5E-05,5.208333333E-11,5.208333333E-11,8.7875E-11,,,+P1
+P1,0.0025,0.0025,-0.0025,0.0025,-0.0025,-0.0025,0.0025,-0.0025,+Q1
+Q1,,,,0.0025
GRID,1,,0.,0.,0.0
GRID,2,,0.05,0.,0.0
GRID,3,,0.1,0.,0.0
CBAR,1,1,1,2,0.0,1.0,0.0
CBAR,2,1,2,3,0.0,1.0,0.0
MOMENT,1,3,,1.,1.0,0.0,0.0
PBAR,2,1,2.5E-09,5.208333333E-19,5.208333333E-19,8.7875E-19,,,+P2
+P2,2.5E-05,2.5E-05,-2.5E-05,2.5E-05,-2.5E-05,-2.5E-05,2.5E-05,-2.5E-05,+Q2
+Q2,,,,2.5E-05
GRID,4,,0.,1.,0.0
GRID,5,,0.0005,1.,0.0
GRID,6,,0.001,1.,0.0
CBAR,3,2,4,5,0.0,1.0,0.0
CBAR,4,2,5,6,0.0,1.0,0.0
MOMENT,1,6,,1.E-06,1.0,0.0,0.0
SPC1,1,123456,1,4
ENDDATA
